WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Calendar

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Story

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Koyomi

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Nothing

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.990
How sloppy.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:41.700
When we fought last summer you had more backbone, didn't you?

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.540
I've pretty much been holding back this time, entirely.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.010
I appreciate that.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.970
Anyway, what are you after...

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.840
challenging me to a fight all of a sudden?

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.470
A lot of things have hit a stopping point for me,

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:05.270
so I thought maybe I'd see if I could get some training from you, Kagenui.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:10.860
I was thinking it'd be nice if, the next time I'm met with a difficult situation,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.900
I could deal with it as deftly as you, and without relying on my vampirism.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.450
Oh, I see. That's what this is about.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.080
But you should probably give up on that.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.370
If you were to try and learn my technique from me like this in live battle practice,

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:31.540
you would die before you learned it.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:39.470
Just why exactly do you think I've sent Yotsugi to invade your house?

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.550
For a little while at least,

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:45.180
I've made it so that you should be able to go without being bothered by oddity affairs.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:54.530
It's just that, it's a little painful going about my day to day life protected by two little girls.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.950
And that is exactly why you can't
carelessly make a move, now isn't it?

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.530
It's the same for <i>them,</i> too.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:09.330
In any case, you shouldn't be doing extreme things like trying to learn anything from me.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:15.050
Why did you get involved with
oddities and ghost stories, Kagenui?

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:20.390
It probably started back in kindergarten, when I punched some irritating kid.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:26.390
Thinking about it now, that brat might have been possessed by some awful thing or another, too.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:31.060
Well, that was from back before I specialized in immortal oddities.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.860
So, the reason you specialize in
taking on immortal oddities now,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.030
is because it's impossible to overdo it, right?

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:44.120
Turning that around, that would mean that you've overdone it quite a lot of times before, wouldn't it?

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.330
Is your profession perhaps based on this?

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.040
I suppose you could say that.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.290
You sure have a lot of questions.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.800
What, do you want me to join as well?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.670
To the fabled 'Araragi harem' or whatever you call it.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.090
<i>Why does she know about that?!</i>

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.680
<i>Er, no. No such scandalous organization actually exists.</i>

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.930
It'd be nice if I could become
enough of a big-shot to woo you.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:12.190
Though right now I'm more worried about staying human than getting big.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:16.190
Don't worry, if you do lose your humanity, I'll be here to beat you to death.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.320
Hey, Kagenui?

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.320
Ash

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.450
What is it?

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:27.450
How are you and Ononoki related to each other?

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.040
My relationship with Yotsugi?

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.710
As you already know, I'm the
exorcist and she is my familiar.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:39.880
But, well, Ononoki <i>does </i>refer to you as 'big sister,' now doesn't she?

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.130
She does.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:45.720
So, I was wondering if you two had a kind of sisterly relationship or something.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.680
If you're gonna say that, it's like this:

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.310
She says big brother when referring to you, too, doesn't she?

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:54.980
She says big brother and big sister when referring to most people.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:55.770
Big brother Oshino

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:56.610
Big brother Kaiki

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.360
Yes... but,

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.990
she calls you just 'big sister.'

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.540
Well, aren't you the perceptive fellow.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:11.870
Or maybe you have good intuition?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.420
Well, it's not really something worth hiding,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.380
and it wouldn't really matter if I told you,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:22.720
but being asked so formally makes me not want to tell you, somehow.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.220
Then, you won't tell me?

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.010
No, I'm not saying I won't.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.180
I also won't charge or put you to work,

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.260
so you can rest easy on that front.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:30.770
Okay then,

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.430
how about a continuation of our battle?

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:35.560
Just one shot.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.230
If you manage to land just one shot while matched against me,

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.190
I'll tell you then.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.950
Yotsugi's true identity.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.320
Magical incantation

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.950
And so that's why, Karen, it's your turn.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.660
Um, what exactly do you mean by 'that's why'?

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.250
<i>I-can't-talk-about-the-details,</i>

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.040
<i>but-there's-this-person-who's-strong-as-an-ox.</i>

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.420
<i>so-strong-that-I'm-utterly-powerless-against-them,</i>

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.710
<i>but-I-want-to-land-a-punch-on-them.</i>

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:58.920
Is there anything I can do?

00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.290
who

00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.290
\{exactly

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.170
\{does

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.170
\{my

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.170
\{brother

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:00.800
\{think

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:00.800
\{ I am?

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.550
I am a martial artist who walks the path of martial arts.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:09.800
Even if I knew a method to practice violence, there's no way I'd teach it to an amateur like you, bro.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.430
Don't talk like that.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.680
I'll fondle your breasts
anytime you like from now on.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:20.190
Oh, really? Well, with a condition like that, then I am also prepared to concede...

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.190
Nothing!

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.280
There <i>is</i> no time when I'd like to get my breasts fondled by my brother!

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.360
Think about it, Karen.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.450
Having your breasts fondled by your brother when you'd like,

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.580
vs. having your breasts fondled when you'd <i>wouldn't</i> like.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.490
Which is better?

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.120
Oh! I'd prefer getting fondled when I'd like!

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.330
It's obvious once you compare them!

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.710
That's my bro, you're so smart!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:42.710
That's my Karen.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:43.590
You're so dumb

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:45.340
Alright, got it.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:50.090
It's not my policy to take on apprentices, but I'll make a special exception for my bro.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.310
So what would you do for example?

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:57.100
If you'd want to land a punch on a person who is clearly stronger than you, what would you do?

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.100
It's impossible!

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.770
No, seriously.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:06.360
Under those terms, it'd be difficult to get in a punch versus that person, wouldn't it?

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.490
Even if it didn't have to be a clean hit.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.700
It'd be difficult even to get in behind their guard, wouldn't it?

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.580
Yeah. I told you, I'm utterly powerless.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.580
If there's such a difference in ability,

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.080
then you just shouldn't fight them.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.830
Martial arts says you should run away.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:25.000
Actually, from what you've told me, I'm guessing it's like this:

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.550
If you can land a punch on this person,

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:30.800
they'll answer a question of yours,

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.180
or something like that, right?

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.890
Yeah, exactly.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.100
That's a pretty good inference coming from you, Karen.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:38.600
Aren't you just being refused indirectly?

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.480
I bet you asked something insensitive.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.230
So maybe you've just been driven away
without being exposed to the sharp edges.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.570
At some point you've started to wonder only about how to land a shot on this person

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:54.370
instead of about whether or not your question will get answered, haven't you?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:00.370
<i>What the?!</i>

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:01.790
I see.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:05.500
So that must be how Kagenui
expresses her adult considerations.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.050
Well in that case, what should I do in response?

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:10.880
How should I know?!

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.010
Think about it yourself!

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.430
But if it<i> were </i>me,

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:20.270
I'd do my best so that this person, who was so considerate of me, wouldn't lose face.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:28.230
At the least, I'd make sure that they didn't find out that I saw through their excuse to propose the fight.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:31.240
<i>So as to give nonchalant concern to Kagenui</i>

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:34.490
<i>by way of hiding my intention to respond to her sentiment,</i>

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.950
<i>I'll need some kind of excuse for when I face her.</i>

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:47.630
<i>So that means I'll have to think of some way to get a shot in on her,</i>

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:50.090
<i>not to win against her, but to lose gracefully.</i>

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:53.970
I'm at a complete standstill.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.680
<i>Now for the epilogue, or rather, the punchline.</i>

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:03.390
<i>To construct a false chance of victory,</i>

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:09.480
<i>I basically followed the same method I took when I fought against her back in summer break.</i>

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.610
<i>As for how I confronted <i>that</i>,</i>

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:15.910
<i>I had Oshino Shinobu suck my blood, boosting the vampirism in both of us,</i>

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.410
<i>strengthening myself, and
then went to confront her.</i>

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.750
This time however, I couldn't use this method as-is.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.830
I can't keep using my vampirism,

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.290
However, I can borrow Shinobu's abilites as much as I want.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.710
<i>I borrowed her ability to materialize matter,</i>

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.170
<i>and had her make me a pistol.</i>

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:33.470
Black

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.640
<i>I brought the handgun only
to use as a tool for rhetoric.</i>

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.430
Donuts

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.430
100-yen sale

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.270
<i>Kagenui said 'one shot.'
</i>

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.140
<i>'If you land one shot.'
</i>

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:49.320
<i>In that case whether that shot was
from a punch or a bullet shouldn't matter.</i>

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:55.950
<i>That's just exactly the kind of simplistic idea that a fool like me would think up.</i>

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.990
<i>And also, and this part's cruicial, it was an idea that would 100% fail.</i>

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.080
<i> An idiotic highschooler stepped up to a game and simply lost.
</i>

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.170
<i>That should be the end of that.</i>

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.670
<i>A sudden response to a nonchalant concern.</i>

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.590
<i>Rather, to counteract my carelessness.</i>

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:19.600
<i>It should at least get a passing grade.</i>

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.430
Ash

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:33.570
Huh?

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:38.320
Huh?

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:43.580
<i>The lifelong undefeated specialist, Kagenui Yozuru, was gone.</i>

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:47.500
Huh?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.000
To be continued

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:15.030
I kick a stone away to get rid of my worries,

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:20.660
I'm downplaying the flutter I feel this April.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:26.160
We were happy children full of curiosity,

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:29.170
I was the one who pushed you forward,

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:32.130
from that day onward.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:37.590
Let's escape our confines

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:43.390
and take our time along the way

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:50.810
Let's ride our bikes to far away

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:56.440
carrying our hopes and dreams in the basket

00:10:56.440 --> 00:11:01.860
Is the future we heard so many rumors about,

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.450
A nice place to be?

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:06.950
Even if we ask our extending shadows about it,

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.660
we'll still be none the wiser

